cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EVSA or ShiftBench-Sim in your research, please cite this work as below."
title: "Evidence-Validated Strategy Adaptation for Memory-Augmented Agents Under Distribution Shift"
authors:
  - family-names: "Parth"
    given-names: "Dev"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Madan Mohan Malaviya University of Technology, Gorakhpur, Uttar Pradesh, India"
date-released: 2026-11-07
version: "2.0.1"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Devparth7-coder/EVSA-Research-Paper"
abstract: >-
  Evidence-Validated Strategy Adaptation (EVSA) is a statistical framework for
  reliable experience validation, applicability-gated retrieval with Safe LGG,
  and per-domain residual CUSUM drift invalidation in memory-augmented agents,
  evaluated in the synthetic symbolic-procedural ShiftBench-Sim v1.0 environment
  with hard capability-isolated oracle separation and reproducible per-family
  and global-74 Holm-Bonferroni statistical ledgers (v2.0.1).
keywords:
  - "memory-augmented agents"
  - "sequential hypothesis testing"
  - "distribution shift"
  - "concept drift detection"
  - "Bayesian credible bounds"
  - "selective memory invalidation"
